A DevTools session that never used the FindInPage domain no longer ends the tab's find session when it detaches.
Chromium 156's new FindInPageHandler::Disable() runs at every detach and called StopFinding(CLEAR_SELECTION) on the
WebContents whenever it had a FindRequestManager, which it has after any find-in-page: the renderer ran "Unselect",
so a selection a script had set in a focused field was gone (selectionStart/End 0,0, no caret) the moment any
session detached. ArdiaCore's own sessions (tab snapshots, cookie reads) detach on their own, so after ⌘F every such call did
this. Disable() now stops only a find this handler started (FindFirst sets query_); FindInPage.stop is unchanged.

diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/find_in_page_handler.cc b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/find_in_page_handler.cc
--- a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/find_in_page_handler.cc
+++ b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/find_in_page_handler.cc
@@ -59,7 +59,9 @@
 
 Response FindInPageHandler::Disable() {
   ResolvePendingCallback(Response::ServerError("Target is being disposed"));
-  StopFindingInternal();
+  if (!query_.empty()) {
+    StopFindingInternal();
+  }
   return Response::Success();
 }
 
